    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Formed on 1 July 1867 by the union of British colonies, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-a-macdonald">John A. Macdonald</a> as its first prime minister.</li><li>It grew by purchase and union into the world’s second-largest country, tied together by the Canadian Pacific Railway.</li><li>It won full independence gradually, through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/statute-of-westminster-1931">Statute of Westminster</a> of 1931 and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constitution-act-1982">Constitution Act, 1982</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odawa">Ottawa</a> was chosen as capital of the Province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a> by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/queen-victoria">Queen Victoria</a> in 1857, partly as a compromise between the rival cities of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toronto">Toronto</a>, Kingston, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shobak-castle">Montreal</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quebec">Quebec</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

